<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24378" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημήτριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		(also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημήτρειος,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημήτρειοι</span>
			), <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Demeter,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					44.5
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καρπὸς Δ.</span> corn, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				2.4.5
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δ. σπέρματα,</span> of
			leguminous plants, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.454
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημήτριος</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μήν</span>), ὁ, month
			in Bithynia, <u>Hemerolog.Flor.</u>: 
				Boeot.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δαμάτριος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				7.296
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.378e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ Δημήτριον</span>”
				<i>the temple of D.,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					9.5.14
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ Δημήτρια</span>”
				<i>her festival,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Poll.
					1.37
				</span></i>
			, etc.; but later, <i>in honour of Demetrius,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Demetr.</u>
				12
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημητρίεια</span></b> , τά, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Supp.Epigr.</u>
				1.362.8
			</span></i>(Samos, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
